# GD-1 (round 19, writer 10): was L2_3_prefixed_band_call; R.b(x) is gone (L §2.3 Calls), so what stays is a band called by a def and an ask.
# Its regime gains is unboxed (the items at top level, gains.x written x); the
# figures are unchanged. The comment below is the old test's.
# L §2.3 Calls (round 14): "A call takes a built-in's name (§2.2) or a band's id, with the prefixes that name the band
# outside its regime ...: R.b(x) for a band regime R exports (§5.17)"; call = (ID {"." ID} ["[" expr "]"] | BUILTIN)
# "(". owed calls fee(amt) from outside gains: amt = 500.00 PLN is in [0, 1 000.00), 10.00 PLN; the ask calls
# fee(big), big = 1 500.00 PLN, 20.00 PLN (L §5.9 rows).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source pit_act "PIT act"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

band fee(x: money PLN): money PLN
band secret(x: money PLN): money PLN

input amt: money PLN
input big: money PLN

def owed: money PLN at reader
  rule base = fee(amt)

version act_2024
  cite pit_act
  governs 2024..
  known 2023-12-01
  amt = 500.00 PLN
  big = 1 500.00 PLN
  fee: [0 PLN, 1 000.00 PLN) = 10.00 PLN
  fee: [1 000.00 PLN, inf) = 20.00 PLN
  secret: [0 PLN, inf) = 1.00 PLN

ask q1: owed, fee(big) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (10.00 PLN, 20.00 PLN)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
